// fmt
// #4752: a bracketed list break that happens inside a width trial the
// formatter then REJECTS is not a break in the output. Counting it left
// `fmtTryChainNestedWrap` (fmtwrap.bit) seeing two breaks where one landed,
// so this chain took the operator wrap on the first pass and the bracketed
// break on the second -- a formatter that needed two passes to reach its
// fixpoint (observed on stdlib/time/business.test.bit at b96932ff).
//
// The trial the count leaked out of is `fmtPrintCommaList`'s own flat trial
// for the OUTER call: rendering it flat pushes the nested
// `businessTestOneHoliday(...)` list over the budget, so that inner list
// wraps, is counted, and is then thrown away with the whole flat render.
fn chainTrialBreak(mon: Day, nextMon: Day) {
  assert(
    mon.differenceInBusinessDays(businessTestOneHoliday(weekendSatSun(), businessTestDate(2026, 9, 16)), nextMon) == 4,
    "one holiday inside the week takes it to 4",
  )
}
